# Line ends the tools need on every checkout, Windows included (core.autocrlf
# would otherwise give them CRLF): the shell scripts run in bash or Git Bash,
# patch(1) applies the flutter_litert patch to LF sources, and
# tool/fetch_models.sh reads the lock line by line. The knowledge-base articles
# keep LF: the prebuilt index is keyed by their bytes, so a CRLF checkout would
# index them again on the device. The Windows launchers keep CRLF, as cmd.exe
# expects.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
tool/models.lock text eol=lf
assets/kb/*.md text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
